		"leaves": {"run": {"at": Vector2(-58.0, 347.0), "prop": "lantern_lit"}, "keep": {"at": Vector2(-58.0, 347.0), "prop": "slabs"}, "name": {"at": Vector2(-58.0, 347.0), "prop": "mark"}},
		"outcome": {"run": "Penn stood on the barn's loft with his tally-stick and counted the water coming down the channel by its sound. 'Running,' he said. 'The Arches have not run since before the Night. They will not run for long. But it will be said, in Fallowmere, that they ran.' He wrote it down in the reeve's book, in his best hand.",
			"keep": "'Shut,' said Penn, and nodded, slowly. 'A reeve knows about shut. You keep a thing shut because the alternative is a flood.' He did not look pleased and did not look sorry. He sat on the barn's step and turned the pin of his own tithe-ledger over, and over.",
