		"text": "The nail is in the witch's door, driven with whatever price you paid, and the farm went on. But a bargain is not a thing that stops when it is struck, Hesper says, and she wants to know what she has been paying for, nine winters, without knowing. Go back to the door. See what is owed. Decide whether it is to be knocked on, or let be, or the nail drawn.",
