					{"key": "nail", "at": Vector2(222.2, 361.4), "name": "the iron nail", "text": "The nail you drove. It has grown a little thorn of rust in the wood, and around it, in a ring, the grain of the door has turned black. Not rot. Writing. The same hand, over and over, round and round: kept."},
					{"key": "step", "at": Vector2(224.0, 362.0), "name": "the worn step", "text": "A step of three stones worn deep in the middle: by feet, not weather. Pairs of feet, a small pair and a pair a woman's width. Both come to the door and neither leaves. Both come again, the same night, in the same order."},
