		"choose": [{"set": "ferryman", "slot": "lantern", "rarity": 2}, {"set": "tally", "slot": "focus", "rarity": 2}, {"set": "bell", "slot": "girdle", "rarity": 2}],
		"leaves": {"leave": {"at": Vector2(223.0, 361.0), "prop": "mark"}, "pull": {"at": Vector2(223.0, 361.0), "prop": "slate"}, "knock": {"at": Vector2(223.0, 361.0), "prop": "lantern_lit"}},
		"outcome": {"leave": "Hesper listened with her arms folded in her apron. 'Stands,' she said. 'Then it is a bargain and not a trap. I can live with a bargain. I have lived with worse.' She went to the door of the farmhouse and fetched the loaf she had been saving, and gave it to you with both hands.",
			"pull": "'Drawn.' Hesper sat down on the step. 'Then it is not paid, and not owed, and I have nothing to be afraid of in the dark, and I am afraid of it anyway.' She laughed at herself, a short shocked laugh. 'Thank you. I should have liked to be the kind of woman who did it herself.'",
			"knock": "'You knocked,' said Hesper, and drew breath, and said nothing for a while. 'And it lit a light.' Her face did something complicated. 'Whatever it is, it was waiting for somebody to ask whether it wanted company. I think I would have been sorry to be the one to find that out.'",
