		"leaves": {"second": {"at": Vector2(299.0, 153.0), "prop": "lantern_lit"}, "take": {"at": Vector2(299.0, 153.0), "prop": "lantern"}, "names": {"at": Vector2(299.0, 153.0), "prop": "page"}},
		"outcome": {"second": "Maudlin held her own hand over the shrine's candle to feel the heat of it. 'Two,' she said. 'Then they are not alone, and nor is the one who keeps the first.' She was weeping, silently, and did not seem to notice. 'The lowest rope used to ring alone. Now there are two. That is a duet. That is a church.'",
			"take": "'You took it back,' said Maudlin. 'Then it is mine again, and I must find out what I meant by it.' She turned it in her fingers. 'It was a good candle. I will light it in the window, toward the road. If they want it, they can come and ask.' She put it in the east window, and it burned all night.",
			"names": "Maudlin knelt, quite suddenly, on the stone of the shrine. 'Their names,' she said. 'Said aloud. The seventh was a boy of eleven.' She put her forehead to the floor. 'I am obliged to you in a way I do not know how to say.' When she rose, she said the names again herself, once, and the shrine's candles burned straight up.",
